## Your task

Partition the runs in this batch into semantically equivalent candidate themes. Each run must contribute to exactly one candidate in its result category, so occurrence counts remain additive and the number of candidates never exceeds the number of runs.

For every candidate:
- Set result to "pass", "fail", or "na" based on the runs in that candidate.
- Include the exact number of matching runs in occurrence_count.
- Preserve 1-3 real generation IDs and one concise representative reasoning example.
- Keep the title concise enough for comparison with candidates from other batches.
- Include every distinct candidate supported by the batch, even when only one run supports it. A theme that is rare locally may be common across the complete evaluation.

Return at most {{ max_candidates }} candidates total.

Do not write an overall assessment, recommendations, global frequency labels, or statistics. The reducer derives those from candidates across every batch.

